uploads_result.json
# `plays/*/data/script.pdf` is NOT here on purpose: it is derived, like manifest.json
# next to it, and committed for the same reason. It is the only derived file whose
# rebuild costs 45 s of LaTeX install, so it is typeset once by uploads.yml when a
# script is actually promoted, rather than on every deployment. ~150 kB per promotion
# enters the history; the mp3s beside it cost far more, and it buys every deploy back.
# The counterpart, and the reason this comment exists: nothing refreshes it at deploy
# time. A script.json edited by hand IN THE REPO leaves a PDF that no longer matches
# the play (cf. scripts/build_script_pdf.py).
#
# The temporary file of the typesetting (`.part` written then renamed, so no reader
# lands on a half-written PDF) stays out: it only survives an interrupted write (full
# disk, runner killed between the two calls), and that is precisely where it must not
# show up in the `git status` of a folder the Action commits whole.
plays/*/data/script.pdf.part
# A play's pages are GENERATED from the templates in `pages/` (one per play and
# per page), in dev as at build time: cf. vite.config.js. Derived and NOT committed,
# unlike the PDF above: seven files per play, identical to its neighbour's, rewritten
# at every config load, and free to rebuild.
plays/*/*.html
